---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { siteSizes, S, sizeUrl } from '../../lib/data';
import { sizeCostPath, sizeMeaningPath } from '../../lib/paths';
import { querySizes } from '../../lib/size-facts';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Sizes', href: '/sizes/' }];
---
<Base title="Tire Sizes Ranked by Treadwear (NHTSA UTQG) | TireMileage" description={`Tire sizes with NHTSA UTQG treadwear rankings. ${S.distinct_explicit_sizes} sizes appear with explicit ratings; ${S.sizes_with_ge5_lines} have at least 5 rated lines.`} crumbs={crumbs}>
  <h1>Tire sizes ranked by treadwear</h1>
  <div class="answer">NHTSA's ratings data names a specific size on {S.records_with_explicit_size.toLocaleString()} of {S.raw_records.toLocaleString()} records, covering {S.distinct_explicit_sizes} distinct sizes. {S.sizes_with_ge5_lines} sizes have 5+ rated lines and {S.sizes_with_ge10_lines} have 10+. This build publishes {siteSizes.length} sizes. Each row links a page for what the code means and a cost-per-mile calculator that uses a quote you type. Some of those sizes have fewer than ten graded lines. The ranking is only the lines NHTSA names for that size. The short list is on <a href="/lookup/">exact tire lookups</a>.</div>
  <div class="tw"><table data-sortable>
    <thead><tr><th>Size</th><th class="n">Rated lines</th><th data-nosort>Exact pages</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{siteSizes.map((s) => <tr><td><a href={sizeUrl(s.key)}>{s.label}</a></td><td class="n">{s.lines}</td><td>{querySizes.some((q) => q.key === s.key) ? <><a href={sizeMeaningPath(s.key)}>What it means</a> · <a href={sizeCostPath(s.key)}>Cost per mile</a></> : '—'}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note"><strong>Coverage limit:</strong> the remaining {S.records_all_sizes_or_range.toLocaleString()} NHTSA records ({Math.round(100 * S.records_all_sizes_or_range / S.raw_records)}%) are filed as “All sizes” or size ranges, so common sizes like 225/65R17 show only the lines NHTSA names explicitly. A tire-size catalog feed is needed to build complete size pages.</p>
</Base>
